      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "Net::CIDR::Lite versions before 0.24 for Perl does not properly validate IP address and CIDR mask inputs, which may allow IP ACL bypass.  Inputs containing a trailing newline or non-ASCII digit characters pass the validators but are then re-encoded by the parser to a different address than the input string spelled. find() and bin_find() can match or miss addresses as a result.  Example:    my $cidr = Net::CIDR::Lite->new();   $cidr->add(\"::1\\n/128\");   $cidr->find(\"::1a\");  # incorrectly returns true  See also CVE-2026-45191.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
